  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building a culture of peace</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will work with young people aged 14-17 in 14 socio-politically marginalized communities, both Palestinian and Jewish, in central Israel. A longer-term component comprising 15 weekly sessions in the local communities and 4 organization-wide activity days aims to encourages the young people to identify injustices relating to their own group as well as &quot;the other,&quot; to initiate efforts to promote social and political change, and to recognize the need to work together to promote a just and equal shared society.  A shorter-term component comprising 8 sessions in the local communities aims to expose youth to social injustices influencing different groups in society, thereby enabling them to recognize the need for social and political change and grasp their own responsibility and ability to work for change.</narrative>
  </description>
